.env
**/.env
**/.venv/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/pytest-cache-files-*/
**/*.pyc
**/*.db
**/storage/
**/*.log
.runtime/
coverage/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
cloudflared.exe

# ── Biometric and identity test data — never committed ──────────────────────
# Face fixtures and UAT evidence are photographs of identifiable people. Git
# keeps deleted files in history forever, so the only safe place for them is
# outside the repository. Point FACE_TEST_IMAGES at one of these directories.
# See docs/TEST-DATA-POLICY.md.
**/tests/faces-local/
**/faces-local/
**/uat-evidence/
**/biometric-evidence/

# Test environment carries real database credentials and secrets. The template
# beside it (.env.test.example) is what belongs in the repository.
**/.env.test

# Playwright run artefacts: traces, screenshots and the last-run summary.
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/

# Claude Code: per-machine permission allowlist, carries local absolute paths.
.claude/settings.local.json

# MCP browser-driver page dumps and ad-hoc verification screenshots. Written
# into the working tree by a debugging session, never an input to the build.
.playwright-mcp/
/*.png

# Timestamped .env backups written by local tooling. `.env` itself is ignored
# above, but `.env.bak-<epoch>` is not matched by that rule, so one had been
# staged for commit carrying PLATFORM_OWNER_PASSWORD, the owner MFA secret and
# every database URL. Secrets in git history cannot be taken back.
.env.bak*
.env.*.bak
*.env.bak

# next 16.3 writes these on every build ("Generated AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md for
# AI agents"). They are build output that restates the installed Next version's
# own guidance, so committing them would put a generated copy of node_modules
# documentation under review and re-conflict on every upgrade. Disable with
# `agentRules: false` in next.config.ts if they are unwanted entirely.
apps/web/AGENTS.md
apps/web/CLAUDE.md

# Locally generated test certificates and keys for the STARTTLS-capable Mailpit
# capture server and the local HTTPS terminator. Regenerate with
# `apps/web/scripts/make-local-tls.sh`; see docs/TEST-ISOLATION.md. Private keys
# never belong in the repository.
apps/web/infra/tls-local/

# Playwright traces record every request and response header of a real signed-in
# session, which means the session cookie and any reset or invitation token that
# happened to be in flight. Useful locally, never in a shared artifact.
validation-evidence/e2e-artifacts/
**/trace.zip
